    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Gunnar Henderson** (65.74) and **Coby Mayo** (61.44), who anchor the lineup as our top-rated plays. Both benefit significantly from a favorable park factor and a high-upside matchup against Shane McClanahan, whose 4.11 xERA suggests he is vulnerable to power hitters. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a platoon disadvantage, the park adjustment and his high-volume role at the #3 spot keep his efficiency well into the elite tier. Similarly, **Coby Mayo** earns a strong projection because the park-adjusted environment mitigates his neutral-to-marginal matchup, and we are counting on his raw power to capitalize on the afternoon conditions. \n\nIn the outfield, **Jackson Merrill** (59.11) and **Kyle Tucker** (58.24) remain essential starts despite the presence of Dean Kremer and Jared Jones on the opposing mounds. **Jackson Merrill** is a focal point for our strategy; despite his raw score, his elite potential to contribute in the scarcest category\u2014stolen bases\u2014makes him a lock for the starting nine. The most difficult decision for today was sidelining **Heliot Ramos** (45.34). While his ability to manipulate opposing pitchers with slow delivery times provides a slight boost to his stolen base upside, he ultimately fell short of the threshold required to displace our current OF depth. The optimizer prioritized the more balanced production profile of **Andy Pages** (52.83) and the high-floor utilization of **Luis Robert Jr.** (53.84), even with the latter\u2019s platoon-related volatility.\n\nWe are currently monitoring \"Lineup Pending\" statuses across the board, which introduces a slight risk to the efficiency scores calculated for **Liam Hicks**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Sam Antonacci**. While their scores assume specific lineup placements, any drop to the bottom of the order could necessitate a re-evaluation of their daily cap usage. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Drake Baldwin** (46.07) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (54.30); they face elite arms in Henderson and Dylan Cease, respectively, meaning their scoring is heavily reliant on the \"xERA-gap\" remaining wide enough to support their high-volume roles. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** sidelined on the IL, our margin for error is razor-thin, and we will continue to monitor weather patterns for any late-breaking wind shifts that could further suppress or inflate these projections.",
